  "text": "Subscribe to skip adsAdvertisementAstronomyThis Photo of the Martian Dawn Could Be Curiosity’s Most Serene Image YetMorning on the Red PlanetDNBy David Nield7:00 AM CDT on October 9, 2026Add Nautilus to GoogleThe Curiosity rover has taken some fantastic photos since it landed on the Red Planet in 2012. And here’s a stunning new one to add to the collection: a view of an early morning Martian sunrise.Powered By 10 ShareNextStayThe shot was captured by Curiosity’s Mastcam, actually two cameras in one snapping images at a resolution of 1,600 by 1,200 pixels. The scene was stitched together from a series of photos snapped at around 8:30 a.m. Mars time on August 11, 2026.The Mastcam is one of many instruments on board Curiosity. Credit: NASA/JPL-CaltechSubscribe to skip adsAdvertisement",
